{%- comment -%}
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Alenok — Portfolio excerpt · Cart line item (Liquid)
  Simplified from the production implementation for demonstration purposes.
  Not a drop-in file: styles, copy, business rules and integrations are omitted.
  © 2026 Fredy Espinoza — All rights reserved. See LICENSE.
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  What this shows
  • Money math on integer cents (Shopify `money` filter)
  • Workaround for a platform limitation: order-level automatic discounts are
    NOT allocated to `item.final_line_price` — only `cart.total_price` has them
  • JSON-safe item keys passed to JS through data attributes
  • Accessible, server-rendered markup that JS progressively enhances
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign reference_unit_cents = section.settings.reference_unit_cents | default: 0 -%}

{%- for item in cart.items -%}
  {%- comment -%} Compare-at reference price scales with quantity {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign ref_cents = item.quantity | times: reference_unit_cents -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    With a single line item, cart.total_price IS the real line price
    (it already includes order-level discounts). With several lines we fall
    back to final_line_price. Trade-off documented in docs/ENGINEERING-NOTES.md.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if cart.items.size == 1 -%}
    {%- assign line_cents = cart.total_price -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign line_cents = item.final_line_price -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- assign save_cents = ref_cents | minus: line_cents -%}

  <div class="cart-item" id="aln-row-{{ item.key }}">
    <div class="ci-img">
      {%- if item.image -%}
        <img src="{{ item.image | image_url: width: 200 }}"
             alt="{{ item.title | escape }}" loading="lazy" width="88" height="88">
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="ci-body">
      <div class="ci-title">{{ item.product.title }}</div>
      {%- unless item.variant.title == 'Default Title' -%}
        <div class="ci-variant">{{ item.variant.title }}</div>
      {%- endunless -%}

      <div class="ci-price-row">
        <span class="ci-price" id="aln-price-{{ item.key }}">{{ line_cents | money }}</span>
        {%- if save_cents > 0 -%}
          <span class="ci-price-old" id="aln-price-old-{{ item.key }}">{{ ref_cents | money }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ci-right">
      {%- comment -%}
        `| json` emits a double-quoted string; putting it in a data attribute
        (instead of an inline onclick="...") avoids quote collisions entirely.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <button type="button" class="ci-remove"
              data-cart-action="remove" data-key='{{ item.key | json }}'>
        Remove
      </button>

      <div class="qty-stepper" role="group" aria-label="Quantity">
        <button type="button" data-cart-action="step" data-delta="-1"
                data-key='{{ item.key | json }}' aria-label="Decrease quantity">−</button>
        <input type="text" inputmode="numeric" readonly
               id="aln-qty-{{ item.key }}" value="{{ item.quantity }}" aria-live="polite">
        <button type="button" data-cart-action="step" data-delta="1"
                data-key='{{ item.key | json }}' aria-label="Increase quantity">+</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endfor -%}
